# EAS Build archives the whole git repo (not just mobile/) so monorepo
# builds can see sibling packages — but this repo also contains
# backend/GENMO (a full PyTorch/CUDA project with model checkpoints and a
# venv, several GB) and supabase/ (SQL migrations, not JS), neither of
# which the Expo app needs at build time. Without this file, EAS falls
# back to .gitignore for exclusions; once this file exists it's used
# INSTEAD of .gitignore, not in addition to it — so the usual excludes
# (node_modules, venvs, build output) are repeated here explicitly.

# Not needed to build the mobile app at all
backend/
supabase/
reference/

# Stray files that landed at the repo root and don't belong in the archive
# (anchored to root only, via the leading slash, so this can't shadow real
# assets anywhere under mobile/)
/IMG_*.PNG
/ScreenRecording*.MP4

# Node / Expo — EAS installs these fresh on its own build servers
node_modules/
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
*.log

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Env / editor
.env
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# mobile/.env IS needed at build time — EXPO_PUBLIC_* vars get baked into
# the JS bundle by Metro during the EAS cloud build itself, which has no
# access to this machine otherwise. Excluding it silently shipped an empty
# Supabase URL/anon key; createClient('', '') throws at module-load time,
# before any UI renders — confirmed as the actual cause of a blank black
# screen on a real TestFlight install, not a hypothetical.
!mobile/.env
